    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d275">

                <pb facs="0396" n="224" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg224"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/3261</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gonzales</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-08T10:00:00-05:29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 8, 1917, 10 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 2.50 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The President has handed me reply of Secretary of State, to my announcement on
                    Sunday of the United States’ action, expressing most cordial sympathy of Cuba
                    for the United States.</p>
                <p>German Government yesterday delivered note to Cuba on the submarine warfare.
                    Pending hearing from you, in reply [<hi rendition="#italic">regard?</hi>] to
                    when expedient to sever relations, they did not take that step, but have sent
                    note of vehement protest opening way for severance of relations.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gonzales</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
